{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_004 (acc=0.5988) using pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat. All four completed experiments share pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, so the RNA encoder dimension is completely unexplored in the best-performing multimodal setup. The image encoder (vit_l > resnet50, ~2% gain) and fusion (concat > weighted with transformer, consistent across both image encoders) are well-established. Question: Does a learned RNA encoder (scgpt) improve over the linear PCA representation when combined with the strongest image encoder and aggregation/fusion stack? This is the largest remaining untested design axis that could yield a meaningful accuracy gain. Why this is the best next experiment: With 5 experiments left, testing the RNA encoder in the best-performing configuration (config_018: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) either opens a new exploitation path (if scgpt helps) or eliminates that dimension so remaining budget can focus on aggregation variants or other refinements. Expected relative cost: scgpt is a full transformer-based generative encoder, so this will be notably more expensive than config_004 (4.76 GPU hrs) — likely ~7–9 GPU hours — but it is the highest-information experiment available and justifiable given the potential accuracy upside."
}

